{
  "dom_id": "step-q169186",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14193755/assets/e597f15091f753a2f3271a6b69d8af9b187835f0a61d1e5109d4e8f588c59e6c.png)\n\nWhich of the shapes above is a regular polygon?",
  "worked_solution": "A regular polygon is a polygon that has the following properties:\n\n- All sides have the same length (i.e., congruent).\n\n- All angles have the same measure (i.e., congruent).\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each polygon in turn:\n\n- Polygon I is not regular. Its sides and angles are *not* all congruent.\n\n- Polygon II is not regular. Its angles are *not* all congruent.\n\n- Polygon III is regular. Its sides and angles are all congruent.\n\nTherefore the answer is \"III only.\"",
